/-!
# Set (c), Stage K, closed forms: the rational coefficients of the branch-1 antiderivative

Helper level (no frozen statement). Step 4 of route D for `ρ_X` (scratch `stageK/STATUS.md`,
session 26+; generated by `stageK/fxg/g1lean.py` from the canonical antiderivative `g1a.py`,
identities checked in `g1c.py`). The `u`-antiderivative `G₁` of `formXJ1L` has rational
coefficients `F_a`, `F̃_b`, `F_c`, `F_d` (of `log(1 - u)`, `(X - u) log(X - u)`,
`log(X + u - Xu)`, `log P`; all with denominator `M²`, `M = coordM X u`), a constant
coefficient `formXG1m` of `log M`, and rational part `formXG1h`. With `ℓ₁ = formXlc1` and
`κ = formXkap`, for `X ∈ (0, 1)`, `u ∈ (0, X)`:

* **`hasDerivAt_formXG1a_piece`**: `(F_a log(1 - u))′ =
  (ℓ₁ + κ(1 - X)/M) log(1 - u) - F_a/(1 - u)`;
* **`hasDerivAt_formXG1b_piece`**, **`hasDerivAt_formXG1c_piece`**,
  **`hasDerivAt_formXG1d_piece`**: the same for the other three letters (coefficient
  `∓(ℓ₁ + κ(1 - X)/M)`).

The derivative of the rational part is `hasDerivAt_formXG1h` (`SetCKFormXG1H`).
-/

@[expose] public section

open Real Set

namespace QED.ChainProof.SetCK

open QED.TwoLoop.UnitSCLimit QED.TwoLoop.UnitLLink

